To solve this problem, you need to implement a **Global Tooltip Provider**.

Since Next.js components are isolated, you cannot rely on local state (like `useState` inside the component) to track which tooltip is open. Instead, you must lift the state up to a Context that wraps your entire application (or the specific layout where you want the tooltip to work).

Here is a complete, copy-pasteable solution using **React Context** and **Tailwind CSS** (standard in Next.js).

### 1. Create the Context and Provider

First, create a file to manage the global state. This will hold the `isOpen` state and the `onClose` function.

**`context/TooltipContext.tsx`**

```tsx
'use client'; // Required for Next.js App Router

import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, ReactNode } from 'react';

// Define the shape of our context
interface TooltipContextType {
  isOpen: boolean;
  setIsOpen: (open: boolean) => void;
  closeTooltip: () => void;
}

const TooltipContext = createContext<TooltipContextType | undefined>(undefined);

interface TooltipProviderProps {
  children: ReactNode;
}

export const TooltipProvider = ({ children }: TooltipProviderProps) => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);

  const closeTooltip = () => {
    setIsOpen(false);
  };

  return (
    <TooltipContext.Provider value={{ isOpen, setIsOpen, closeTooltip }}>
      {children}
    </TooltipContext.Provider>
  );
};

// Custom hook to use the context
export const useTooltip = () => {
  const context = useContext(TooltipContext);
  if (!context) {
    throw new Error('useTooltip must be used within a TooltipProvider');
  }
  return context;
};
```

### 2. Wrap your Application

You need to wrap your app so the context is available everywhere. In Next.js App Router, this is usually done in `layout.tsx`.

**`app/layout.tsx`**

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import { TooltipProvider, useTooltip } from "@/context/TooltipContext";
import "./globals.css";

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "Next.js Global Tooltip",
  description: "Generated by create next app",
};

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: Readonly<{
  children: React.ReactNode;
}>) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {/* Wrap children in the Provider */}
        <TooltipProvider>
          {children}
        </TooltipProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

### 3. Create the Tooltip Component

This component reads the context to know if it should show or hide.

**`components/Tooltip.tsx`**

